  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Bellou Toilettage is run by Alexandra, a qualified groomer with 14 or 15 years of experience depending on the source (a slight discrepancy, perhaps from a recent update), in an air-conditioned, secure salon on place Adolphe Béguin, in the La Serinette district of Toulon. The salon isn't limited to dogs: it also welcomes rabbits, guinea pigs and birds, and has a hoist with a safety harness for lifting large dogs into the bathtub — confirmed by the official website (belloutoilettage.fr).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The salon is known for its stress-free atmosphere, a real plus if your dog (or rabbit) tends to get anxious about grooming — one regular customer of over 10 years says they even bring two Belgian Malinois there. By appointment, Tuesday to Saturday. Prices are given over the phone after a few questions about the animal, finalised on the day of the appointment — no fixed price list is published.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your companion is scared of the hairdryer or salon noises, mention it when booking — the stress-free atmosphere is precisely their strong point.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon and its wider area offer plenty of options for the rest of the day, between the town centre and the seafront.</p>
